---
title: Mac & Cheese
description: A creamy, three-cheese gluten-free mac and cheese baked with a buttery cracker topping for the ultimate comfort food.
course: side
cuisine: American
servings: 8
time required: 1 hour
prep time: 30 minutes
cook time: 30 minutes
source: https://sweetandsavorymeals.com/gluten-free-mac-and-cheese/
image: https://sweetandsavorymeals.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Gluten-Free-Mac-and-Cheese-Recipe-5.jpg
tags:
  - gluten-free
  - pasta
  - cheese
  - comfort-food
  - baked
---

Preheat the oven to 350°F and lightly grease a #9x13 baking dish{} and set aside.

In a #large pot{}, cook @gluten-free elbow macaroni{1%lb} to al dente, then drain and rinse under hot water. Toss with @olive oil{1%tbsp} in a #large bowl{} and set aside.

In a #large saucepan{} over medium heat, melt the @unsalted butter{4%tbsp}. Add the @gluten-free all-purpose flour{1/4%cup} and whisk until fully combined.

Gradually add @milk{5%cups} while whisking until smooth.

Add the @onion powder{1%tsp}, @garlic powder{1%tsp}, @paprika{1%tsp}, @mustard powder{1%tsp}, @red pepper flakes{1/4%tsp}, and @salt{1/4%tsp}.

Bring to a boil over medium heat and simmer for ~{2%minutes}.

Stir in the @sour cream{1/2%cup} and adjust @salt{} and @pepper{} to taste.

Reduce the heat to low and add the @sharp cheddar cheese{2%cups}(grated), @white Colby cheese{1%cup}(grated), and @Parmesan cheese{1%cup}(grated), stirring until melted.

Combine the sauce with the cooked pasta, then transfer the mixture to the prepared baking dish.

For the topping, mix the @gluten-free buttery crackers{1 1/2%cups}(crushed) with @melted unsalted butter{6%tbsp}.

Sprinkle the reserved @white Colby cheese{1%cup}(grated), @cheddar cheese{1/2%cup}(grated), and @Parmesan cheese{1/2%cup}(grated) evenly over the top, then add the buttery cracker topping.

Bake uncovered until golden brown and bubbly, ~{30%minutes}.

Rest for ~{15%minutes} before serving.
